Microsoft's <stdio.h> defines printf and scanf inline, over _vfprintf_l, _vfscanf_l and the two __local_stdio_*_options functions with their static ?_OptionsStorage@... objects, so cl's object carries those six names; this tree's <cstdio> declares both and leaves them to the library. The names this case is about - a::twice through b::twice to ::twice - agree: ?twice@a@@YAHH@Z on both sides.
